WEBVTT

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:11.845
What?

00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:13.763
I can see your blind spot!

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:16.474
Come on!

00:00:16.474 --> 00:00:18.226
I'll crush you, Uza-Uza!

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:19.894
Shit!

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:22.147
Is this the best you can do?

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:24.357
Come on! Bring it on!

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:27.068
Middle school cowards!

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:29.738
Ahh... Ecstasy!

00:00:31.656 --> 00:00:34.951
All of you are still moving horribly.

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:39.622
One shot with all my soul!

00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:42.459
Too bad!

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:43.793
Try again next week!

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:50.216
If I don't get a shuffle match soon,
I can't move up!

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.221
Each court is getting better.

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:58.308
Perhaps they've been inspired
by the middle schoolers.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.061
The high schoolers have been
full of spirit, as well.

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:04.314
Especially since the losers returned.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.738
Try harder!

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:31.549
Soon we'll overthrow Court 1!

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.761
Just thinking about it is getting me excited!

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.221
Right, Koshimae?

00:01:37.138 --> 00:01:38.640
If you're just thinking about it,

00:01:39.516 --> 00:01:41.559
you still have a long way to go!

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:21.326
"Prelude to a Revolution"

00:03:24.996 --> 00:03:29.042
The effects of including middle
schoolers in this training camp

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.336
exceeded our expectations.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.588
Don't be so sure.

00:03:35.131 --> 00:03:37.967
They should be on their way here now.

00:03:38.635 --> 00:03:40.136
Finally...

00:03:41.137 --> 00:03:45.100
Not even we can predict
what will happen next.

00:03:51.981 --> 00:03:53.066
Super lame!

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.568
Nice hit, Echizen.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:55.985
Thanks.

00:03:56.361 --> 00:03:58.655
Shishido, put more effort into it!

00:03:58.655 --> 00:04:00.407
Shut up! I know!

00:04:00.407 --> 00:04:03.576
Okay, Koshimae! Play me next!

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.413
Attention, players.

00:04:06.413 --> 00:04:08.665
Today's practice is now over.

00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:10.750
Hey, hang on!

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.253
I haven't played Koshimae yet!

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.758
Please gather on the main
court for an announcement.

00:04:19.134 --> 00:04:20.927
An announcement?

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.848
Tomorrow morning,

00:04:25.223 --> 00:04:27.517
we will announce the 20 athletes,

00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:30.770
out of these 146, who have
been selected for strengthening.

00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:36.192
Selected for strengthening?

00:04:36.568 --> 00:04:38.528
The selected athletes

00:04:38.528 --> 00:04:42.115
will begin training on their
own courts as of tomorrow.

00:04:43.324 --> 00:04:45.577
On their own courts, huh?

00:04:46.161 --> 00:04:48.038
I guess training camp is almost over.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:49.664
You are dismissed.

00:04:49.664 --> 00:04:51.124
Good work today.

00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:52.959
Thank you very much!

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:55.545
Selected athletes, he said!

00:04:55.545 --> 00:04:58.715
Koshimae, who do you think they'll choose?

00:04:58.715 --> 00:05:01.551
They'll obviously pick me.

00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:03.887
They're obviously gonna pick me, too!

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.807
Are you guys not heading back?

00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:10.477
In a minute.

00:05:11.269 --> 00:05:13.396
Steel your resolve, everyone.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.315
Our resolve?

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:19.778
This training camp will become
even more brutal tomorrow.

00:05:21.905 --> 00:05:23.281
It's about time.

00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:25.492
They can make it as brutal as they want.

00:05:25.492 --> 00:05:26.910
I welcome it.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:30.580
Exciting, isn't it? I'm getting really fired up.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.749
Compared to the battle starting tomorrow,

00:05:33.249 --> 00:05:36.920
the training we've done until now
was no more than a warm-up.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.838
A warm-up?

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:42.258
Hell would quite possibly be easier.

00:05:42.676 --> 00:05:44.386
We're not trying to scare you,

00:05:44.386 --> 00:05:45.929
but the real battle starts tomorrow.

00:05:46.971 --> 00:05:48.515
The real battle?

00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:49.849
I look forward to it.

00:05:50.266 --> 00:05:52.644
You guys still don't understand...

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:57.774
the true terror of this training camp.

00:05:58.149 --> 00:05:59.776
True terror...

00:06:00.276 --> 00:06:04.656
Now, now... Either way,
you'll find out tomorrow.

00:06:19.087 --> 00:06:22.799
The winners' meals are the best!

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:24.759
Kintaro, try this!

00:06:24.759 --> 00:06:27.762
It's good! It's oozing juices!

00:06:27.762 --> 00:06:29.431
Thanks, Momo-<i>chan</i>!

00:06:30.849 --> 00:06:33.727
Awesome! This really is the best!

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.856
Hey, where did the losers train?

00:06:37.856 --> 00:06:39.399
On top of a cliff.

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:41.234
I already heard about that!

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.861
You didn't even have power, right?

00:06:42.861 --> 00:06:44.320
What'd you do at night?

00:06:47.699 --> 00:06:48.867
We used torches.

00:06:48.867 --> 00:06:51.119
Torches? Seriously?

00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:52.787
What is this, the Stone Age?

00:06:54.456 --> 00:06:56.166
Quiet, Kirihara.

00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:57.709
What's the problem?

00:06:57.709 --> 00:06:59.669
I'm the only one who doesn't know!

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:02.756
So what kind of secret training did you do?

00:07:02.756 --> 00:07:05.008
I heard it was life-threatening!

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:07.093
Secret training?

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:08.428
Who told you that?

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.849
Did you get chased by giant
metal balls or anything like that?

00:07:14.517 --> 00:07:16.269
We were chased by eagles.

00:07:16.644 --> 00:07:17.687
Man-eating eagles?

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:19.606
No.

00:07:19.606 --> 00:07:22.692
We competed with the high
schoolers to keep the eagles

00:07:22.692 --> 00:07:24.361
from popping balloons tied to our waists.

00:07:24.361 --> 00:07:28.490
Seriously? You didn't lose to
the high schoolers, did you?

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:29.908
Of course not.

00:07:30.784 --> 00:07:32.535
We overthrew them.

00:07:32.535 --> 00:07:34.371
Ooh! And, and, and...

00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:35.538
What else?

00:07:35.538 --> 00:07:36.748
All kinds of stuff.

00:07:36.748 --> 00:07:40.752
What kind of stuff? That's what I'm asking!

00:07:40.752 --> 00:07:42.671
Ask the others.

00:07:44.005 --> 00:07:45.882
You're so cold...

00:07:45.882 --> 00:07:47.092
Right, Kaidoh?

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:52.430
What, you too?

00:07:57.936 --> 00:07:59.854
What is he doing?

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.830
Zaizen! Hey, Zaizen!

00:08:17.956 --> 00:08:19.916
You're so noisy.

00:08:19.916 --> 00:08:20.750
What do you want?

00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:23.962
You weren't here at first, right?

00:08:23.962 --> 00:08:26.089
When did you join the camp?

00:08:26.089 --> 00:08:30.468
I met up with the losers on their way
up the cliff and stuck with them.

00:08:30.468 --> 00:08:32.512
Me and Yuji-<i>senpai </i>both.

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:33.179
Why?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:34.597
I don't know.

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:37.017
You don't know?

00:08:38.268 --> 00:08:40.603
The food here is not bad,

00:08:40.603 --> 00:08:43.440
but still I miss homemade food of my country.

00:08:43.815 --> 00:08:45.817
What's your favorite dish?

00:08:45.817 --> 00:08:47.027
Miso soup.

00:08:48.695 --> 00:08:50.447
It's a Japanese dish.

00:08:50.739 --> 00:08:52.615
Hey, Koshimae.

00:08:52.615 --> 00:08:56.369
I can't understand a thing if
you keep speaking in English.

00:08:56.703 --> 00:08:59.914
But I think miso soup
here is a little strong.

00:09:00.582 --> 00:09:01.458
Right.

00:09:01.458 --> 00:09:05.211
Koshimae! I'm bored!

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:06.671
--Bored, bored, bored!

00:09:06.671 --> 00:09:08.131
--So...
--Bored, bored, bored!

00:09:08.131 --> 00:09:11.051
--Toyama-<i>kun</i>, what do you like?
--Bored, bored, bored!

00:09:11.051 --> 00:09:13.219
That'd be tennis and takoyaki.

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:14.137
I see.

00:09:14.387 --> 00:09:16.056
What about you?

00:09:16.723 --> 00:09:18.516
Well, of course, tennis and...

00:09:18.516 --> 00:09:20.977
Yeah! Tennis is great!

00:09:21.353 --> 00:09:22.354
Okay, bro!

00:09:22.354 --> 00:09:24.147
Let's play a match right now!

00:09:24.439 --> 00:09:28.318
Now? I don't know...

00:09:28.318 --> 00:09:30.153
Let's play! Let's play!

00:09:30.445 --> 00:09:32.781
What? Um, I...

00:09:32.781 --> 00:09:34.741
Now sounds good.

00:09:35.241 --> 00:09:36.326
Nice idea.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:39.537
Why are you getting changed?

00:09:39.913 --> 00:09:41.498
We'll play, too.

00:09:41.498 --> 00:09:42.540
Night game.

00:09:43.375 --> 00:09:44.125
What?

00:09:44.125 --> 00:09:46.211
Now it's getting interesting!

00:09:46.211 --> 00:09:47.879
Come on, bro!

00:09:48.129 --> 00:09:50.298
Wh-What?

00:09:50.965 --> 00:09:53.259
What's wrong with those three?

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:55.929
They just do whatever they please...

00:09:55.929 --> 00:09:59.140
Don't look at me with those glittering eyes.

00:10:00.266 --> 00:10:01.559
But, well...

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:05.647
They're better than
Mizuki-<i>san</i>'s devious eyes.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:11.361
Here I go, Shishido-<i>san</i>!

00:10:11.361 --> 00:10:12.987
Bring it on, Chotaro!

00:10:16.241 --> 00:10:17.117
There!

00:10:18.159 --> 00:10:19.494
Wait, you two!

00:10:19.911 --> 00:10:21.705
That pillow fight looks fun!

00:10:21.705 --> 00:10:23.081
Let me join you!

00:10:23.081 --> 00:10:25.834
Don't, Eiji. You'll send dust flying everywhere.

00:10:26.584 --> 00:10:31.798
But I didn't get to join in the last
pillow fight. I missed all the fun!

00:10:32.132 --> 00:10:33.508
Didn't you hear them?

00:10:33.508 --> 00:10:34.926
Training will be even more brutal to--

00:10:37.679 --> 00:10:41.516
Let's see which of us
is the real Golden Pair!

00:10:42.851 --> 00:10:43.935
So that's it...

00:10:46.187 --> 00:10:48.481
I can't turn down a challenge.

00:10:50.734 --> 00:10:53.069
You saw the ghost of a deserter?

00:10:54.112 --> 00:10:57.240
Yeah, a ghost! It's true!

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.242
So, you said a warding incantation?

00:10:59.242 --> 00:11:02.454
Yeah! "Skip Skip Iguana Bang!"

00:11:02.829 --> 00:11:05.123
What kind of cheap incantation is that?

00:11:05.123 --> 00:11:09.002
No, really! Apparently this area
used to be a battlefield!

00:11:09.002 --> 00:11:09.878
Isn't that freaky?!

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:13.173
I can't believe that scares you.

00:11:13.173 --> 00:11:14.799
Right, Kaid--

00:11:19.137 --> 00:11:21.556
Kaidoh's terrified.

00:11:21.931 --> 00:11:23.641
Now I've got something to blog about.

00:11:25.018 --> 00:11:26.102
Wait.

00:11:26.478 --> 00:11:30.899
This place is a battlefield
with ghosts of deserters.

00:11:31.441 --> 00:11:33.818
I read about this in a book.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.195
Right?

00:11:35.653 --> 00:11:38.907
"Skip Skip Iguana Bang."

00:11:38.907 --> 00:11:41.618
So it was true...

00:11:41.618 --> 00:11:44.079
But the incantation didn't work!

00:11:44.079 --> 00:11:46.706
It suddenly floated out of...

00:11:47.707 --> 00:11:49.084
What's wrong, Kaidoh?

00:11:50.502 --> 00:11:51.586
I gotta use the bathroom!

00:11:54.673 --> 00:11:57.008
He's scared. This is hilarious.

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:00.470
Synchronization?

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:02.097
They're using that now?

00:12:02.597 --> 00:12:07.936
That's a rare doubles miracle that
only occurs in desperate situations!

00:12:09.187 --> 00:12:11.439
Shishido-<i>san</i>, I'm scared!

00:12:15.235 --> 00:12:16.528
I'm not scared.

00:12:16.528 --> 00:12:17.904
I'm not scared!

00:12:18.363 --> 00:12:19.781
There's no deserter here!

00:12:23.034 --> 00:12:23.618
Ultimate technique!

00:12:24.536 --> 00:12:26.413
So Ba Ga Ra!

00:12:37.966 --> 00:12:39.050
Damn it, Kaidoh!

00:12:39.467 --> 00:12:40.885
What are you doing?

00:12:44.305 --> 00:12:46.558
Don't scare me!

00:12:51.855 --> 00:12:53.898
What the heck?

00:12:55.025 --> 00:12:56.818
You guys go to sleep early.

00:13:05.827 --> 00:13:07.078
Buckwheat husks <i>(sobagara)</i>...

00:13:07.454 --> 00:13:10.665
Aren't you guys taking this a bit far?

00:13:10.665 --> 00:13:12.917
What? You're the one who started it!

00:13:13.293 --> 00:13:15.837
No way! You guys were first!

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:19.758
You're making too much noise, fools!

00:13:22.677 --> 00:13:24.888
Kabaji, make them be quiet.

00:13:26.931 --> 00:13:27.849
Kabaji?

00:13:29.267 --> 00:13:31.019
Good work, Kabaji.

00:13:31.019 --> 00:13:32.020
Puri.

00:13:33.188 --> 00:13:34.814
"Niou Kingdom"
"Kabaji      Niou"

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:39.235
What is this plant called?

00:13:39.235 --> 00:13:41.738
Monkshood. It's poisonous.

00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:43.031
Poisonous, huh?

00:13:43.531 --> 00:13:46.242
Does it take away the five senses?

00:13:46.242 --> 00:13:48.203
More than just that.

00:13:50.455 --> 00:13:53.375
Yukimura, your daisies are beautiful, as well.

00:13:54.417 --> 00:13:57.170
They're tough against environmental changes,

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:58.880
so they're relatively easy to grow.

00:13:59.673 --> 00:14:03.343
Fuji-<i>kun</i>, your cactus looks
like it'll bloom soon.

00:14:03.343 --> 00:14:04.386
Yeah.

00:14:06.054 --> 00:14:09.224
I'm glad they let us bring plants.

00:14:09.224 --> 00:14:12.227
They all wilted while I was in the hospital.

00:14:12.644 --> 00:14:17.065
But now, new life is born again.

00:14:17.065 --> 00:14:18.066
Yeah.

00:14:18.775 --> 00:14:21.152
The next generation takes over.

00:14:23.321 --> 00:14:23.988
Bro!

00:14:24.322 --> 00:14:25.907
Another pillow fight is starting!

00:14:26.241 --> 00:14:27.826
We should take shelte--

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:29.244
Yuta-<i>kun</i>!

00:14:32.622 --> 00:14:34.624
I'm going to go for a little workout.

00:14:38.253 --> 00:14:39.337
Need a hand?

00:14:40.255 --> 00:14:42.507
Was that Jackal-<i>kun</i>?

00:14:42.882 --> 00:14:44.926
I'm not done yet!

00:14:47.846 --> 00:14:48.638
This time...

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:51.516
I will win!

00:14:52.183 --> 00:14:52.600
I will...

00:14:54.185 --> 00:14:55.687
defeat him!

00:14:58.064 --> 00:14:59.190
I will!

00:15:04.195 --> 00:15:06.656
They're working hard so late at night.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:10.702
The team touring abroad?

00:15:11.119 --> 00:15:13.079
This camp's first string.

00:15:13.455 --> 00:15:17.876
They're all stronger than the Court 1 guys.

00:15:18.126 --> 00:15:21.296
Tomorrow, they're returning
from a one month tour.

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:26.092
So the players selected for strengthening...

00:15:26.092 --> 00:15:30.221
They'll come up with something to
test the guys who stayed behind.

00:15:31.431 --> 00:15:35.560
He said we should make
the most of this opportunity.

00:15:36.936 --> 00:15:38.730
Make the most of it...

00:15:39.356 --> 00:15:41.983
Well, I've relayed my message.

00:15:52.702 --> 00:15:54.496
I'm getting fired up now!

00:15:57.749 --> 00:15:58.958
Not bad, Kaidoh!

00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:00.627
You haven't missed once!

00:16:01.169 --> 00:16:03.546
There's no point in playing if you don't win!

00:16:03.546 --> 00:16:04.589
I agree!

00:16:04.964 --> 00:16:06.132
Come on!

00:16:06.132 --> 00:16:07.717
We're not done yet!

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:16.393
Vice Captain, good work.

00:16:16.935 --> 00:16:20.939
What are you doing?

00:16:20.939 --> 00:16:23.566
Um, it wasn't just me!

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:24.984
The others were...

00:16:24.984 --> 00:16:27.070
Wait, what?!

00:16:29.239 --> 00:16:32.450
Y-You are...

00:16:33.326 --> 00:16:34.661
...going soft!

00:16:36.371 --> 00:16:38.081
You won't get away with this!

00:16:38.081 --> 00:16:40.917
What do you think this camp is for?

00:16:40.917 --> 00:16:42.544
--Are you celebrating every
day because you won?

00:16:42.544 --> 00:16:44.212
--No fair...
--Are you celebrating every
day because you won?

00:16:44.212 --> 00:16:46.423
--Pillows are for supporting
your head when you sleep!

00:16:46.423 --> 00:16:48.133
--Hilarious.
--Pillows are for supporting
your head when you sleep!

00:16:53.013 --> 00:16:56.266
I will now announce the players
selected for strengthening.

00:17:06.943 --> 00:17:08.111
Why?

00:17:08.111 --> 00:17:10.488
"U-17 Second String Selection, 20 Members"
Why these 20?

00:17:10.488 --> 00:17:12.240
I don't accept this!

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:14.200
Yeah, all the players they chose

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:16.077
are high schoolers.

00:17:16.077 --> 00:17:20.874
We've won more shuffle
matches than they have!

00:17:20.874 --> 00:17:21.791
But...

00:17:23.084 --> 00:17:25.295
Just one middle schooler was chosen...

00:17:27.172 --> 00:17:31.718
Well, well... What is a middle
schooler doing here?

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:35.638
You don't seem to understand
what this place is.

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:41.353
So, shall we begin?

00:17:42.437 --> 00:17:43.938
Considering their strength,

00:17:43.938 --> 00:17:48.026
it's no wonder members from
Courts 1 to 3 were chosen.

00:17:48.026 --> 00:17:50.236
But this is different.

00:17:50.236 --> 00:17:52.906
You mean there's a reason?

00:17:53.656 --> 00:17:56.618
The coaches play dumb,

00:17:56.618 --> 00:17:58.745
but it's clear they're up to something.

00:18:06.002 --> 00:18:07.003
Pathetic...

00:18:07.962 --> 00:18:09.464
Rikiya,

00:18:09.464 --> 00:18:11.424
prepare their coffins.

00:18:13.802 --> 00:18:16.388
You two, come on out here.

00:18:21.309 --> 00:18:22.435
You're...

00:18:22.852 --> 00:18:27.148
the middle schoolers who recently
joined the training camp, right?

00:18:27.649 --> 00:18:29.192
You're an eyesore. Beat it.

00:18:31.361 --> 00:18:33.947
Oh? You wanna go?

00:18:40.787 --> 00:18:43.790
You're going to abandon
your unconscious teammates?

00:18:45.625 --> 00:18:48.503
I won't let you get away with that!

00:19:08.523 --> 00:19:09.899
Damn you!

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.361
Welcome back,

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:15.280
Akiba-<i>kun</i>.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:22.203
You shouldn't bully the weak.

00:19:22.203 --> 00:19:23.788
It's not nice.

00:19:31.671 --> 00:19:32.714
I see.

00:19:33.089 --> 00:19:35.925
Coach Nyudo told them about
the team touring abroad.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:39.637
So they decided to strike first.

00:19:44.851 --> 00:19:46.728
M-Momoshiro's missing!

00:19:47.062 --> 00:19:49.356
So is Yanagi-<i>senpai</i>!

00:19:49.356 --> 00:19:51.149
Oishi's missing, too!

00:19:51.608 --> 00:19:54.152
So are several others!

00:19:55.278 --> 00:19:59.366
I can't believe I didn't notice.
Kinda lame of me.

00:19:59.783 --> 00:20:02.452
Victory goes to the swiftest.

00:20:02.827 --> 00:20:04.579
It's the standard formula.

00:20:04.996 --> 00:20:08.500
From now on, our court numbers
don't matter anymore.

00:20:09.959 --> 00:20:12.420
It's all-out war.

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:15.340
Steel yourselves and let's go!

00:20:18.635 --> 00:20:21.930
You knew about the first string.

00:20:22.514 --> 00:20:23.640
Vaguely.

00:20:24.808 --> 00:20:27.519
I thought you'd be the first to go.

00:20:28.144 --> 00:20:29.604
I'm surprised you stayed.

00:20:31.314 --> 00:20:34.025
It seemed like staying would be more fun.

00:20:41.241 --> 00:20:43.827
Their spirits break after
playing the first string.

00:20:45.078 --> 00:20:48.623
Every year, about half of the
guys drop out at this point.

00:20:50.917 --> 00:20:52.168
What about you?

00:20:52.627 --> 00:20:56.965
I'm staying here to settle a score.

00:20:58.466 --> 00:21:01.636
This definitely seems more fun.

00:21:04.889 --> 00:21:05.807
They're...

00:21:06.307 --> 00:21:07.976
...already on the move.

00:21:09.644 --> 00:21:11.896
Go play with them.

00:21:14.691 --> 00:21:15.734
Just so you know,

00:21:16.651 --> 00:21:18.486
none of us are dropping out.

00:21:19.946 --> 00:21:21.823
Our captain told us...

00:21:23.366 --> 00:21:25.744
We'll see this through until the end.

00:21:26.244 --> 00:21:27.912
All of us.

00:21:35.587 --> 00:21:39.174
I hope you're not all talk.

00:21:39.174 --> 00:21:41.760
Of course not. We...

00:21:44.679 --> 00:21:45.597
...will win.

00:23:18.398 --> 00:23:19.816
"Next Time"

00:23:19.816 --> 00:23:21.860
"Next Time"
I never imagined we'd play
like this, Akuto-<i>niisan</i>.

00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:24.571
I never imagined we'd play
like this, Akuto-<i>niisan</i>.

00:23:24.571 --> 00:23:26.448
It's been a while, Renji.

00:23:26.448 --> 00:23:27.574
Today, I won't--

00:23:27.574 --> 00:23:29.784
"Today, I won't hold back."

00:23:29.784 --> 00:23:31.244
That's what you're going to say.

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:33.913
You're eager enough,

00:23:33.913 --> 00:23:36.708
but your tennis won't work against me.

00:23:36.708 --> 00:23:39.336
I'll show you what real
Data Tennis looks like.

00:23:42.130 --> 00:23:44.758
"The Battle Begins"
The next episode of <i>New Prince </i>
<i>of Tennis </i>is: "The Battle Begins."

00:23:44.758 --> 00:23:48.480
